§§ `6–9 המענק`

-- §6: the management may approve a grant to a teaching employee absent for
-- illness who (א) has used the accrued sick leave he had, days carried from
-- earlier employers under the agreements included; (ב) is permanent,
-- temporary or on a special contract and has completed a year of actual
-- teaching; (ג) was in an employer's service the day the accrued days ran
-- out, a substitute on a monthly salary included; (ד) was absent for
-- illness for seven consecutive days at least after they ran out; (ה) has
-- used the special sick leave of §9 below, if the State gave him one.
@desc A teaching employee asking the fund of 10.9.2003 for a grant.
DECLARE `fund application of 10.9.2003` HAS
    `used the accrued sick leave, carried days included` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permanent, temporary or on a special contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed a year of actual teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an employer's service the day the accrued days ran out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a substitute on a monthly salary included
    `consecutive days absent ill after the accrued days ran out` IS A NUMBER
    `was given the special sick leave of §9` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used the special sick leave of §9` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_6 akn:art_6__para_a akn:art_6__para_b akn:art_6__para_c akn:art_6__para_d akn:art_6__para_e
GIVEN a IS A `fund application of 10.9.2003`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund of 10.9.2003 may approve a grant` a IF
        a's `used the accrued sick leave, carried days included`
    AND `the conditions ב to ה of §6 of 10.9.2003 hold` a

GIVEN a IS A `fund application of 10.9.2003`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conditions ב to ה of §6 of 10.9.2003 hold` a IF
        a's `permanent, temporary or on a special contract`
    AND a's `completed a year of actual teaching`
    AND a's `in an employer's service the day the accrued days ran out`
    AND a's `consecutive days absent ill after the accrued days ran out` AT LEAST 7
    AND (a's `used the special sick leave of §9` OR NOT a's `was given the special sick leave of §9`)

-- §7: the payments weigh the teacher's economic and social situation and
-- are at most 100% of the salary he would have been paid on ordinary paid
-- sick leave. §10: the payment is computed on that salary.
@ref akn:art_7 akn:art_10
GIVEN `the grant the management sets` IS A NUMBER, `the salary as on ordinary paid sick leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the fund's grant of 10.9.2003` `the grant the management sets` `the salary as on ordinary paid sick leave` IS
    min `the grant the management sets` `the salary as on ordinary paid sick leave`

#ASSERT `the fund's grant of 10.9.2003` 12000 10000 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the fund's grant of 10.9.2003` 6000 10000 EQUALS 6000

-- §8: the grants run, as a rule, for at most 3 consecutive months; §18
-- lets the management go beyond it.
@ref akn:art_8
GIVEN `consecutive months asked` IS A NUMBER, `the management makes an exception under §18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant period of 10.9.2003 is allowed` `consecutive months asked` `the management makes an exception under §18` IF
    `consecutive months asked` AT MOST 3 OR `the management makes an exception under §18`

-- akn:art_9 The frame of §9: a label row with no text of its own.

-- (א): the agreement does not take away sick leave on half the salary, at
-- the Treasury's expense and ex gratia, for up to three months, on the
-- Civil Service Commission's special approval — the special sick leave §6(ה)
-- asks to be used first.
@ref akn:art_9__para_a
`the most months of the special half-pay sick leave of 10.9.2003` MEANS 3
`the special sick leave of 10.9.2003 pays a share of the salary of` MEANS 1/2
`the agreement of 10.9.2003 leaves the special half-pay sick leave in place` MEANS TRUE

-- (ב): no grant for a period of illness already paid for under another
-- collective agreement or arrangement on a sick-days fund.
@ref akn:art_9__para_b
GIVEN `paid for the period under another sick-days fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a grant of 10.9.2003 is barred for the period` `paid for the period under another sick-days fund` IF
    `paid for the period under another sick-days fund`

-- The Sick Pay Law (imported), §§4, 5 and 12. A teaching employee's sick
-- pay is a collective agreement's, so §1 leaves him out of "an employee"
-- and §§2–6 do not reach him; compared all the same, so that nothing turns
-- on reading §1. The fund does not stand in for sick pay: it pays only once
-- the accrued sick days the agreements give have been used (§6(א)), and
-- those are at least §4's at every point — 30 days a year with no ceiling
-- under the takanon's §1.25.3.1 and circular תשע"ג/5, weighed there,
-- against §4's 18 and its 90 — so by then §4 leaves nothing (the days used
-- are the law's own under §12(א), which gives sick pay on one ground of
-- the employee's choice, not on both). Seven days' wait (§6(ד)), a grant the
-- management weighs and may set below the salary (§7), and its three months
-- (§8) are therefore above the floor: the law gives nothing then. What a
-- grant is computed on (§10) is §5's measure; and §4א, which reaches a
-- teacher, protects his accrued days, of which the agreement says nothing.
GIVEN `full months worked for the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `accrued sick days the agreements gave him, all used` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of sick pay the law still owes when the fund of 10.9.2003 may pay` `full months worked for the employer` `accrued sick days the agreements gave him, all used` IS
    `days of sick pay section 4 leaves him` `full months worked for the employer` `accrued sick days the agreements gave him, all used`

`the fund of 10.9.2003 pays only past the Sick Pay Law's days` MEANS
        NOT `an employee as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` TRUE
    AND all (GIVEN m YIELD `days of sick pay the law still owes when the fund of 10.9.2003 may pay` m (m TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 12) EQUALS 0) (LIST 1, 12, 36, 240)
    AND all (GIVEN m YIELD `days of sick pay the law still owes when the fund of 10.9.2003 may pay` m (min `most days of sick pay section 4 lets accrue` (m TIMES `days of sick pay a full month of work accrues under section 4`)) EQUALS 0) (LIST 1, 12, 36, 240)
    AND `the fund's grant of 10.9.2003` 99999 10000 EQUALS `sick pay section 5 gives` 10000
#ASSERT `the fund of 10.9.2003 pays only past the Sick Pay Law's days`

§§ `10–12 חישוב המענק ומעמד התקופה`

-- §10, the salary a grant is computed on, is encoded with §7 above.

-- §11: the payment is gross; the compulsory payments any law requires or
-- allows to be deducted are deducted from it.
@ref akn:art_11
GIVEN `the gross grant` IS A NUMBER, `deductions the law requires or allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the net grant of 10.9.2003` `the gross grant` `deductions the law requires or allows` IS
    `the gross grant` MINUS `deductions the law requires or allows`

-- §12: the period a grant is paid for is sick leave without salary; it
-- counts for promotion and seniority (the civil-service regulations'
-- §33.215), not for severance pay or a pension.
DECLARE `purpose a fund period of 10.9.2003 may count for` IS ONE OF
    `promotion, of 10.9.2003`
    `seniority, of 10.9.2003`
    `severance pay, of 10.9.2003`
    `a pension, of 10.9.2003`

@ref akn:art_12
`a grant period of 10.9.2003 is sick leave without salary` MEANS TRUE

GIVEN p IS A `purpose a fund period of 10.9.2003 may count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a grant period of 10.9.2003 counts for` p IF
    p EQUALS `promotion, of 10.9.2003` OR p EQUALS `seniority, of 10.9.2003`

#ASSERT NOT `a grant period of 10.9.2003 counts for` `severance pay, of 10.9.2003`

§§ `13–16 הבקשה, האישור והתשלום`

-- §13: the application. (א): on a special form, by the teaching employee,
-- through the organisation, the district offices (for state employees) or
-- the employer concerned. (ב): the organisation's representatives note
-- their remarks on it and send it to the teaching personnel section of the
-- district the teacher is placed in (a state employee), which checks and
-- confirms the facts, completes the rest and sends it on to the managing
-- committee; another employer's approval comes first. (ג): the Ministry
-- of Labour and Welfare's teaching employees, by the same rules, through
-- its personnel section.
DECLARE `channel for an application of 10.9.2003` IS ONE OF
    `through the organisation, of 10.9.2003`
    `through the district offices, for state employees, of 10.9.2003`
    `through the employer concerned, of 10.9.2003`

@ref akn:art_13 akn:art_13__para_a akn:art_13__para_b akn:art_13__para_c
GIVEN `a state employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `employed by the Ministry of Labour and Welfare` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `who checks an application of 10.9.2003 before the management` `a state employee` `employed by the Ministry of Labour and Welfare` IS
    BRANCH IF `employed by the Ministry of Labour and Welfare` THEN "the personnel section of the Ministry of Labour and Welfare"
           IF `a state employee` THEN "the district's teaching personnel section"
           OTHERWISE "the employer, before the forms go to the management"

-- §14: the approval goes, (א) for a state employee, to (1) the teacher,
-- (2) the district manager, (3) the district's education treasurer, (4) the
-- institution, (5) the organisation; ¶2: the district treasurers pay, at
-- the latest 45 days after the management approved; (ב) for one who is not
-- a state employee, to (1) the teacher, (2) the employer, (3) the
-- organisation, (4) the school's management; ¶2: the employer pays, and
-- sends the accounts, every expense of it included (national insurance,
-- employer's tax and the like), to the head of the conditions-of-service
-- department to be reimbursed.
@ref akn:art_14 akn:art_14__para_a akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_14__para_a__subpara_5 akn:art_14__para_b akn:art_14__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_14__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_14__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_14__para_b__subpara_4
GIVEN `a state employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `how many the approval of 10.9.2003 is sent to` `a state employee` IS
    IF `a state employee` THEN 5 ELSE 4

@ref akn:art_14__para_a/p2
`paying a state employee's grant of 10.9.2003` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `pay a grant the fund of 10.9.2003 approved`
    WITHIN 45
    LEST  BREACH BY `the State` BECAUSE "הסכם 10.9.2003 §14(א): district treasurers pay a grant at the latest 45 days after the management approved it"

@ref akn:art_14/p2
`paying another employer's teacher's grant of 10.9.2003` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay a grant the fund of 10.9.2003 approved`
    HENCE (PARTY `the conditions-of-service department`
           MUST  `reimburse the employer for a grant of the fund of 10.9.2003`)

-- §15: the papers sent to the teacher with the approval and the payments
-- say that the grant is a special grant of the teaching employees'
-- sick-days fund, run jointly by the employers and the organisation, and
-- that in the period it pays for the teacher is on sick leave without
-- salary. §16: the management keeps the applications and copies of the
-- approvals in its archive, and copies go into the teachers' personal files.
@ref akn:art_15 akn:art_16
`the papers of 10.9.2003 name the grant and the unpaid sick leave` MEANS TRUE
`the approvals of 10.9.2003 are kept and filed` MEANS TRUE

§§ `17–21 חשבונות הקרן, חריגים, חידוש, חילוקי דעות ותחילה`

